The final timing audit found 98 cost-run exits after their scheduled 30-minute boundary. For 79, the boundary minute is absent, so the frozen fallback to the next observed source minute applies; the longest wait is 3,100 minutes across a market closure. For 19, the boundary open exists but the preceding minute needed to submit a native `NEXT_BAR` order is absent, so the native engine exits one minute late. I’m recording these as a material execution deviation; I will not label the run an exact replay of that exit rule.
